DATA = """
Cartord is a marketplace where buyers shop from independent sellers. Prices are shown in Nigerian naira. Buyers, sellers, and administrators each have their own account and dashboard.

How do I sign in? Open Sign in. Choose the Buyer or Seller tab, then enter your username and password. After a buyer signs in, Cartord opens the shop. A seller goes to the seller dashboard. Administrators use their own sign-in and land on the admin overview.

How do I create an account? Choose Get started on the public site, or Sign up. To sell, choose Sell in the top bar or Start selling in the buyer sidebar, which opens seller sign-up.

How do I browse or search for products? Choose Shop in the top bar, or the search icon at the top of a buyer or seller dashboard. The shop page has a search box and a sort control. Open a product from the results. The product page has a link back to all products.

Where is the buyer menu? On a computer, the buyer pages use a left sidebar. On a phone, use the menu button at the top. The entries are Dashboard, My Orders, My Cart, Wishlist, Notifications, and Settings. Log out is at the bottom of that menu. The Cartord logo returns to the buyer dashboard.

How do I get back to the dashboard? Choose Dashboard in the sidebar, or Back to dashboard from the assistant chat. The search icon in the dashboard header opens the shop.

Where do I see my orders? Buyers open My Orders in the sidebar. That page lists each order with the product, quantity, price, date, and status. The buyer dashboard also shows recent orders and a link to view all of them.

Where is my cart and how do I check out? Open My Cart in the sidebar, or the cart icon in the top bar while you are shopping. The cart page is where you change quantities, remove items, and place the order. Each cart line becomes its own order and is paid from your wallet.

Where is my wishlist? Open Wishlist in the buyer sidebar. A heart on a product saves it. Saved items stay in this browser only.

Where do I see my wallet balance? Buyers do not have a separate Wallet page. The balance is the Wallet balance card on the buyer dashboard. Sellers see earnings on the seller overview, and can also open Wallet in the seller sidebar.

How do I update my profile, address, or password? Buyers open Settings in the sidebar. That page is My profile, with full name, email, and shipping address. The username is shown there but cannot be edited. The password form is on the same page. Sellers open Store & profile for account details and the password form.

How do I open the assistant? On the buyer dashboard, choose Ask the AI assistant. A chat button is also available on the dashboards. From the public site, AI assistant is in the top bar before you sign in. Inside the chat, Back to dashboard leaves the conversation. New chat starts a fresh conversation.

How do I sell on Cartord? From a buyer account, choose Start selling at the bottom of the sidebar. Sellers use the left sidebar: Overview, Products, Inventory, Orders, Sales analytics, Wallet, Notifications, and Store & profile. Add a product from Products. Change stock from Inventory. The search icon still opens the shop.

What do the seller Orders, Sales analytics, and Notifications pages show? Those sidebar links exist, but seller order lists, sales charts, and an in-app notification inbox are not available yet. The sales figure a seller can see today is the wallet balance on Overview. Notification email is sent separately.

Checkout places one order for each cart line. The order service checks the current price and stock, reserves the quantity, and pays from the buyer's Cartord wallet. A successful payment confirms the order. A failed payment cancels the order and releases the reserved stock.

Order status is one of pending, confirmed, shipped, delivered, cancelled, or failed. Buyers see their orders under My orders. Money spent counts delivered orders only. Pending, confirmed, and shipped orders are still active.

Sellers create and edit listings from Products. A new product needs a name, description, price, and available stock. The inventory service assigns the SKU, and the SKU cannot be changed later. Product images must be JPEG, PNG, or WebP, at most 5 MB each, and at most 5 images per product.

The shopping assistant can explain where to click, look up the customer's own orders and wallet balance, and change the signed-in customer's shipping address. Placing a new order is done from My Cart, not by the assistant. The assistant must not invent products, prices, stock, orders, or account figures it has not fetched.
""".strip()
